---
permalink: sitemap.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{#-
  Two exclusions, and they are two because this site hides a page in two
  different ways. Most content is hidden by swapping its layout to
  excluded.njk (see .eleventy.js's eleventyComputed), which the first test
  catches. Scene-POV pages don't use that mechanism - they keep their own
  layout and gate their body on `item.included`, set per character in
  _data/scenePovPages.js - so without the second test a narrowed clone
  advertised its hidden POV placeholders as real content.
-#}
{#-
  Two builds list nothing at all.

  A SITE_NOINDEX build (a testing or staging domain) because its robots.txt is
  already `Disallow: /` and every page carries `noindex, nofollow` - so a
  sitemap here enumerates pages the same domain has just said not to index. It
  was unreachable rather than harmful, since robots.txt omits the Sitemap line
  and disallows the file itself, but shipping a list of URLs we are actively
  hiding is the wrong artifact to leave lying in a document root.

  And a non-ranking member of a tier family (lib/editions.js's `ranksAt`) lists
  nothing. Every page it serves canonicals to the family's ranking domain, and
  a sitemap advertising URLs we have just told Google not to index is
  contradictory signalling - Google's own guidance is to keep non-canonical
  URLs out of sitemaps. src/robots.njk drops its Sitemap line to match, so
  nothing points at the empty file either.
-#}
{%- if not site.ranksAt and not site.noindex %}
{%- for entry in collections.all %}
{%- if entry.data.layout != "excluded.njk" and (not entry.data.item or entry.data.item.included) and entry.outputPath and entry.outputPath.endsWith(".html") %}
  <url><loc>{{ entry.url | absoluteUrl(site.url) }}</loc></url>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
</urlset>
